    "body": "A correction of the wording, from a read of the pin (context pack; nothing was run).\n\nThe pin `outside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock` measures engagement, not leftover material. Its helper `late_entry_cut` counts the stock that the moves that are not planar (plunges, helices, lead-ins) cut after the first floor feed. The assert is `late < 1.0` mm2, and it reads 332.88 mm2 on `main`.\n\nThus the fault is: with Pass starts at Outside, a later entry of 2D Offset comes down into uncut stock at the full tool width. That is a tool-load fault (the cutter can break). No material stays on the part after the operation because of it. The title says \"leaves uncut stock\"; read it as \"enters uncut stock\".\n\nFacts for the worker:\n- The red pin is not on `main`. It is in the closed PR #3439 (`327cf6bba:crates/motion/tests/pass_start_engagement.rs`, lines 179-215). Draft PR #3566 ports the four sibling pins that pass.\n- The one place that selects the landing of a later pass is `lead_in` in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/level_order.rs` (lines 247-257). It looks at cut vertices in 0.9 tool radii only. That this reach is too short for a ring one stepover away is a reading, not a measurement.\n- The Auto path, the Inside start and the fallback warning law must not change.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
