    "body": "Escalation from issue-worker-high. The work is an open design question, not a fix at one place. I raise the label to `effort:max` and release the claim.\n\nWhat I measured (worktree `issue-3442`, base `6cfc0a6d4`):\n\n1. The pin `outside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock` (ported from #3439 into `crates/motion/tests/pass_start_late_entry.rs`) is red on main at **332.88 mm2**.\n2. The pack's reading holds. `lead_in` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/level_order.rs:247-257`) never finds a landing for this case. A print of each later pass start (D8, stepover 4) gives these results:\n   - 8 later passes, all with `lead None`.\n   - The nearest cut walk is at **4.00 mm** for each start (one stepover). The search reach is 0.9 r = 3.6 mm.\n   - The nearest cut vertex is at 4.22 mm to 39.95 mm.\n3. Each later pass starts at a dead end on the part wall. Example: ring 2 starts at (14.73, 12.00), on the centre-area circle of R 19. The climb sense fixes the walk direction, so the end of each piece is next to the end (not the start) of the next ring. A tangent lead into the start in the walk direction must come from the part side, and that side is the part keep-out. Thus each later start has a crescent of uncut stock, one stepover deep, in front of the tool.\n\nTwo fixes that I tried. Each one breaks a pin on main:\n\n- **A. Planar lead across one stepover** (`lead_across`: land on the nearest point of a cut walk within 2 x 0.9 r, then a straight feed to the start). The pin goes to **0.00 mm2**, with no fallback. But the lead feeds into the crescent at the full tool width. These tests in `crates/motion/tests/pass_start_levels.rs` go red:\n  - `outside_band_split_by_the_part_cuts_no_move_at_full_width`: max cut width 7.985 mm > 5.15 mm at (17.23, 8.30).\n  - `outside_band_with_a_do_not_touch_pin_cuts_no_move_at_full_width`: 8.000 mm > 5.15 mm at (21.59, -4.00).\n  - `the_wall_first_and_narrow_cases_are_named_on_the_path`: the horseshoe cavity gets the new cold-entry fallback in place of the narrow note.\n- **B. No landing means the named fallback** (Auto order, a note with `RINGS_FALLBACK`). The pin is refused (the plan is Auto). The Auto order slots the band, so the same two shape-mask tests go red (8.000 mm > 5.15 mm at (-30.75, -3.90)), and the band notes test sees the fallback note.\n\nMain today posts a plunge or helix at each dead-end start. The shape-mask law measures planar feeds only, so main passes it, and the late pin counts the entry. The late pin (no stock cut by a non-planar move) and the shape-mask law (no planar feed wider than one stepover) cannot both hold at a dead-end start under the climb sense. #3439 passed its pin with planar leads, because its sibling pins average the width over a window of 3 R. Main's shape-mask test reads the maximum width.\n\nA decision is necessary before code. These are possible directions:\n- Accept a ramp along the pass as the entry at a dead end, and let the pin count only plunges and helices that are wider than one stepover.\n- Change the order of the pieces (for example, a reversed walk at a dead end, which breaks climb), with a decision entry.\n- Accept a short planar radial lead, and let the shape-mask law allow it.\n\nHeld work: branch `issue/3567-outside-later-entry`, commit `12c0fd125` (not for merge). It has the ported red pin, option A (`lead_across`, `cold_entry` in `LevelPlan`, `entry_fallback_note` in `pass_start.rs`) and two unit pins in `level_order_tests.rs`. No PR is open.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
