    "body": "Priority raised from `P3` to `P2`.\n\nChosen: `P2`. A silent wrong result is the class that `P1` and `P2` cover. The operation leaves 332.88 mm2 of stock uncut and posts no warning. A user does not see the gap until the part is finished. The workaround is to cut the area again by hand, so `P3` was too low.\n\nDropped: leaving the label at `P3`. That would put the defect behind the current `P3` set while the merged 2D Offset Outside law keeps under-cutting.\n\nEffort stays `effort:high`, which meets the safety floor for a change that can move a toolpath.\n\nThe pin that found this comes from PR #3439, which was closed as already implemented by #3353. Pin PR #3566 keeps the pins that pass on main's law.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
