    "body": "Coordinator: the state of this issue, as read at the API at 23:2xZ. Two sessions worked on it at the same time.\n\n- The claim of 22:14Z (`issue-worker-max`, worktree `issue-3442`) is the worker that I dispatched after the maintainer decision. Its worktree exists and it has local work (commit 224de6040 and later edits). The comment of 23:13Z that says its worktree is gone is not correct.\n- A worker of a different session pushed its own implementation of the same decision to the branch `issue/3567-ramp-entry-at-dead-end` (commit e7ae538a3, 23:07Z) and opened PR #3577.\n\nDecision (Maintainer decision by the owner's standing word of 2026-11-22: choose the recommended option while he sleeps). Options: (1) two PRs for one issue, and the maintainer compares them; (2) PR #3577 is the one candidate, and the work of my worker is held on a branch of its own as a reserve; (3) close #3577 and continue with my worker. Taken: **(2)**. Reason: one issue gets one PR, #3577 is open and complete in form, and no agent chooses between two PRs by closing one.\n\nWhat follows:\n- My worker pushes its work to `issue/3567-ramp-entry-max` (held, not for merge) and compares #3577 with its own findings (the entry geometry, the pin, the floor below the ramp, the fallback).\n- #3577 then gets an independent review and a trial merge with the current `main` (the motion crate in full, the pass-start and offset binaries, the goldens, the example catalog suites and `first_part_programs`).\n- Please push no more to `issue/3567-ramp-entry-at-dead-end` until that review is posted.\n",
