    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T23:24:41Z",
    "body": "For the maintainer, in the morning: one fact about the decision \"a ramp along the pass at a dead end\".\n\nAt a dead end one stepover of uncut stock is in front of the tool and the part wall is behind it. The ramp along the pass thus cuts a slot at nearly the full tool width while it goes down (about 83 percent of the tool disc is in uncut stock at each of the 8 starts of the test case), at the ramp angle of the entry or 3 degrees. After the ramp the pass cuts at one stepover, as before. This is a normal entry in CAM practice, and the full-width law of the tests does not measure it, because that law reads planar feeds only (#3581).\n\nMaintainer decision (owner's standing word 2026-11-22: choose recommended while he sleeps). Options: (1) accept the full-width ramp at the ramp angle and state it in the decision file, the PR and the changelog; (2) stop the work until the maintainer confirms; (3) find an entry that never cuts at the full width (it needs the reversed walk that the maintainer dropped). Taken: **(1)**. Reason: it is what \"a ramp along the pass\" gives by geometry, the angle limits the load, and the alternatives were dropped in the decision. If the maintainer wants a lower load, the ramp angle of the operation is the control.\n\nPR #3577 is reviewed (comment on the PR): four items to fix and the gate to complete. The coordinator's worker makes the changes on that branch.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
