    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T00:29:25Z",
    "body": "Coordinator: two corrections and one decision, from the worker that made the review fixes of PR #3577 (measured, not read).\n\n## Correction of the \"full width\" statement\nMy comment above said that about 83 percent of the tool disc is in uncut stock at a dead end. That number is 332.88 mm2 divided by 8: the stock that each helix of `main` cut over its whole orbit. It is not the disc at the start of the ramp. Measured on the pin grid: about 25 percent of the disc (12.6 of 50.3 mm2) is uncut stock where each of the 8 ramps of the band case starts, and the band width that the ramp cuts is 4.78 mm for a tool of 8 mm (the limit of the tests is 5.375 mm). So the ramp of the band case is NOT a slot at nearly the full tool width. The decision file of the PR carries the measured numbers. The earlier decision (\"accept the ramp\") stands; its reason is better than I wrote.\n\n## A cost defect that blocks the merge\nWith the ramp, the verifier takes minutes: #3588 (`band_reach` slices the model at each different cut Z, and each ramp move has its own Z). The app test `fig8_pocket_outside_starts_each_level_at_the_stock_edge` takes 89.6 s on `main` and more than 1500 s on the PR head. The planning itself takes 0.21 s.\n\n## Decision (Maintainer decision by the owner's standing word of 2026-11-22: choose the recommended option while he sleeps)\nOptions: (a) push the review fixes now, keep PR #3577 a draft, and fix the verifier cost in its own issue first; (b) hold all work on the PR until the verifier fix merges; (c) make the ramp coarse so that it has few planes (the ramp then leaves the proved pass). Taken: **(a)**. PR #3577 does not merge before #3588 is fixed and `pocket_pass_start` runs in a normal time. The workaround for users stays: Pass starts at Auto.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
